cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this benchmark result, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ExergyNet Achieves 76.2% Accuracy on LongMemEval-S with 91.6% Lower Context Consumption"
type: report
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
url: "https://exergynet.org/research-edt-bench-001.html"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ezumba/exergynet-research"
abstract: >-
  EDT-BENCH-001 evaluates ExergyNet's xLMP Semantic Router against the LongMemEval-S
  benchmark (500 questions, 6 question types) using session-level BM25 and an
  evidence-only Oracle as comparators. xLMP achieved 76.2% accuracy (381/500 correct)
  with a mean of 2,456 provider-reported prompt tokens per query — a 91.6% reduction
  versus session-level BM25 (29,382 tokens/query, 56.4% accuracy). The 1.8
  percentage-point difference between xLMP and the Oracle (74.4%) was not
  statistically significant (McNemar exact two-tailed p = 0.474, n = 500).
  Evaluation used gemini-3.8-flash for both generation and evaluation.
  This is a single-run evaluation; a turn-level BM25 granularity control (B4)
  has not been conducted.
